  <h1>About DaoismHub</h1>
  <p class="lede">Last updated: October 19, 2026 &middot; Applies to daoismhub.com and data.daoismhub.com</p>

  <h2>What this site is</h2>
  <p>
    DaoismHub is an educational reference about Chinese contemplative traditions — articles,
    translations, data records and practitioner reports on meditation theory and practice.
    It is built for readers, researchers and practitioners who want a structured, sourced
    entry point to the tradition.
  </p>

  <h2>Editor &amp; Author</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Ding.W</strong> — a meditation practitioner dedicated to sharing traditional
    Chinese meditation theory and the experience of fellow meditators with the world.
  </p>
  <p lang="zh">
    禅修练习者，致力于分享中国传统禅修理论和其他禅修者的经验到世界。
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Email: <a href="mailto:martinwang2024@gmail.com">martinwang2024@gmail.com</a> —
    corrections, sourcing questions and collaboration inquiries welcome. See the
    <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> for details.
  </p>

  <h2>Editorial standards</h2>
  <p>
    Content follows evidence-first practice: sources are cited inline, records carry data
    tier and update stamps, and traditional terminology is explained rather than asserted.
    Read the <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a> for the site's scope and limits.
  </p>

